# 15_decode_mqa_logits_int64.patch
#
# FIX: int32 byte-offset overflow in the FP8 paged MQA-logits DECODE kernel.
#
# GLM-5.3-Flash-FP8 decode crashes at ~64K context on MI300X (gfx942) with a
# "Memory access fault" / EngineDead (NOT OOM). Root cause: the Gluon paged
# decode kernel computes per-KV-page byte offsets  idx * stride_k_seq  (and the
# scale sibling  idx * stride_scale_seq )  in int32. At >64K tokens the KV /
# scale buffers exceed 2^31 elements (VLLM_SPARSE_INDEXER_MAX_LOGITS_MB=4096 =>
# 2^30 f32 elems; KV cache up to 4 GB), so the product wraps past 2^31 and the
# load/store hits an illegal address. Prefill survives because its sibling
# kernel (fp8_mqa_logits.py) was already widened; the OUTPUT store here was too
# ( (pid_batch*next_n+pid_next_n).to(tl.int64)*stride_out_batch ) but the KV /
# scale READ base offsets were left int32.
#
# Fix: widen the per-page ROW/PAGE base offset to int64 at the offset site,
# keeping the inner column/tile offset int32 -- mirroring (a) the already-fixed
# output store in this same file and (b) the maintainers' own already-widened
# reads in the _preshuffle "if" branch, which use gl.load(... .to(gl.int64) ...).
# AMD buffer_load uses a 32-bit hardware voffset and cannot address >2^31, so
# tensor-index reads are converted to gl.load with an int64 element offset;
# scalar-index reads fold the widened page base into the buffer_load/store base
# pointer (leaving the small in-page offset in the 32-bit voffset).
#
# All three reachable Gluon variants are patched:
#   _gluon_deepgemm_fp8_paged_mqa_logits            (KVBlockSize=1, block_size==1)
#   _gluon_deepgemm_fp8_paged_mqa_logits_preshuffle (block_size>1)
#   _gluon_deepgemm_fp8_paged_mqa_logits_preshuffle_varctx
# The host wrapper (rocm_aiter_mla_sparse.py: rocm_fp8_paged_mqa_logits) selects
# Preshuffle = block_size > 1, and the preshuffle kernels branch on
# LoadBlockIndiceForEachStage (the "if"/"else" arms), so any of them can run.
#
# NOTE ON PATH: verify the installed file path before applying. These Gluon
# kernels import from aiter.ops.triton.gluon.pa_decode_gluon, so the file is
# expected at  <site-packages>/aiter/ops/triton/gluon/pa_mqa_logits.py .
# If your aiter build ships them as  aiter/ops/triton/pa_mqa_logits.py  (the
# module the host imports), rewrite the a/ b/ headers below accordingly. aiter
# v0.1.19.
#
